WEBVTT

00:06:27.829 --> 00:06:30.621
or La Española, as they called it then.

00:06:30.663 --> 00:06:34.413
Things were not good:
food was scarce, disease was rampant

00:06:34.454 --> 00:06:37.329
and Columbus may not have been
the best manager,

00:06:37.371 --> 00:06:38.913
so mortality rates were high.

00:06:38.954 --> 00:06:40.413
And by the 1980s and 90s,

00:06:40.454 --> 00:06:43.163
when archaeologists began
to excavate the settlement

00:06:43.204 --> 00:06:44.454
and then the cemetery,

00:06:44.496 --> 00:06:45.788
they started to wonder:

00:06:45.829 --> 00:06:49.621
Did the ships’ rosters include
everyone who is buried here?

00:06:49.663 --> 00:06:51.621
Who actually lived at La Isabela?

00:06:52.621 --> 00:06:54.746
My job came a bit later
as a graduate student

00:06:54.788 --> 00:06:56.996
when I was tasked
with going around the island

00:06:57.038 --> 00:07:00.371
to try and collect samples that could
serve as proxies for human teeth.